<title>USA: Dow Jones industrial average rises 50 points.</title>
<headline>Dow Jones industrial average rises 50 points.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average rose more than 63 points at midday Monday, breaking out of a narrow trading range that followed last week's string of record highs.</p>
<p>Shortly after 2 p.m. EDT, the 30-share Dow was up 63.18 points at 8,176.62, which activated the New York Stock Exchange's limits on program trading.</p>
